# Server

## Outbox Events

### Heartbeat

> Used to signal to the other peer that the connection is still up.

```json
{
    "ttl": <int>
}
```

- `ttl`: How long the client should keep the connection open after this heartbeat.

### Message

> Used to send chat data to a client.

```json
{
    "counter": <int>,
    "private": <bool>,
    "timestamp": <int>,
    "author": <String>,
    "content": <String>
}
```

- `counter`: Increasing chat-message counter.
- `private`: Whether this is a private message or a lobby message.
- `timestamp`: Server timestamp when the message arrived.
- `author`: Nickname of the message author.
- `content`: Message contents.

### ForcedDisconnect

> Used to notify a client that it has been disconnected.

```json
{
    "reason": <int>,
    "message": <String>
}
```

- `reason`: ID of the disconnect cause.
- `message`: Optional user-facing explanation.

### Notification

> Announces lobby changes, such as players joining, state changes, game completion, or a winner being selected.

```json
{
    "counter": <int>,
    "type": <int>,
    "lobby": <LobbyState>
}
```

- `counter`: Increasing lobby-notification counter.
- `type`: ID of the lobby update type.
- `lobby`: Serialization of the new lobby state.

### Update

> Announces a game-state change.

```json
{
    "counter": <int>,
    "game_state": <GameState>
}
```

- `counter`: Increasing game-state update counter.
- `game_state`: Serialization of the new game state.

### Error

> Signals that a client event could not be processed.

```json
{
    "id": <int>,
    "type": <int>,
    "message": <String>
}
```

- `id`: ID of the event that caused the error.
- `type`: ID of the error type.
- `message`: Error description.

### Ok

> Signals that a client event was accepted.

```json
{
    "id": <int>
}
```

- `id`: ID of the accepted event.

## Inbox Events

Inbox events are sent by clients to the server. Every event has a unique client-generated `id`.

### Heartbeat

> Keeps the client connection alive.

```json
{
    "id": <int>
}
```

### Message

> Sends a chat message.

```json
{
    "id": <int>,
    "private": <bool>,
    "recipient": <String>,
    "content": <String>
}
```

- `private`: Whether the message is private.
- `recipient`: Nickname of the recipient when `private` is `true`.
- `content`: Message contents.

### DisconnectAlert

> Requests that the client disconnect from the server.

```json
{
    "id": <int>,
    "reason": <int>
}
```

- `reason`: Client-provided disconnect reason.

### NotificationOffer

> Requests a lobby action that changes lobby state.

```json
{
    "id": <int>,
    "type": <int>,
    "data": <String>
}
```

- `type`: ID of the requested lobby action.
- `data`: Action-specific parameters.

### Offer

> Offers a game action to the server.

```json
{
    "id": <int>,
    "type": <int>,
    "data": <String>
}
```

- `type`: ID of the game action.
- `data`: Action-specific parameters.

## Player State

A player is a client connected to the server. A player's nickname is unique outside the current match and remains associated with that client across lobbies.

```json
{
    "nickname": <String>,
    "connected": <bool>
}
```

- `nickname`: Globally unique player nickname.
- `connected`: Whether the player currently has an active connection.

## Lobby State

The lobby contains players before and during a match.

```json
{
    "state": <int>,
    "players": [
        <PlayerState>
    ]
}
```

- `state`: Current lobby-state number.
- `players`: List of players in the lobby.

